### 6. ⚠️ Hardcoded Data / No Environment Config *(OWASP A05 – Security Misconfiguration)*

**Problem:** User data is hardcoded directly in the route handler. In a real app secrets, connection strings, and config must come from environment variables — never source code.

**Fix:**
```js
// BEFORE — data/config baked into source
const PORT = 3000;

// AFTER — driven by environment with a safe default
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
const JWT_SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET;
if (!JWT_SECRET) throw new Error('JWT_SECRET environment variable is required');
```

---

### 7. ⚠️ No CORS Policy *(OWASP A05 – Security Misconfiguration)*

**Problem:** No CORS headers are set. If this API is consumed by a browser client, the default "open" behaviour (or framework defaults) may allow any origin to make credentialed requests.

